    "title": "Marshall Space Flight Center to lose hundreds of employees - NewsBreak",
    "text": "HUNTSVILLE, Ala. (WHNT) — According to POLITICO , at least 2,145 senior-ranking NASA employees, including hundreds of employees at the Marshall Space Flight Center, are set to leave their jobs. POLITICO writes that MSFC will lose 279 employees, out of the 2,145 total who are set to leave. The online publication said these employees are in GS-13 to GS-15 positions. These are senior-level government ranks normally reserved for those with specialized skills or management responsibilities. This is due to the Trump administration’s plans to reduce the federal workforce, according to documents obtained by POLITICO. President Trump’s proposed 2026 budget includes cuts to NASA’s staff and budget. POLITICO writes that NASA has offered staff members early retirement, buyouts and deferred resignations in response to these plans. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WHNT.com.",
